%% Sequence 02b1 — DONE completion orchestration
%% Updated: 2026-07-29.
%% Scenario: the subordinate Command owns the complete ordered mutation inside its caller's transaction.
%% Evidence status: Implemented.

sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant P as «control» Parent status Command
    participant C as «control» CompleteTaskAssignmentsCommand
    participant A as «outbound» TaskAssignmentRepository
    participant R as «outbound» TaskReviewReader
    participant E as «outbound» TaskAssignmentCompletionEventWriter
    participant T as «transaction» Caller-owned transaction

    P->>C: execute(taskId, assignedTo, changedBy, T)
    activate C
    C->>A: completeActiveForTask(input, T)
    A-->>C: completed assignments
    C->>R: ensureTaskReviewWorkflow(taskId, changedBy, T)
    R-->>C: workflow ensured
    loop each completed assignment
        C->>E: stage(typed completion event, T)
        E-->>C: staged in domain outbox
    end
    C-->>P: completion mutation ready
    deactivate C
    Note over P,T: Parent decides when DONE invokes completion and owns COMMIT/ROLLBACK
